.TH DNSSEC-SIGN 1 "2026-08-18" "rgbdns 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dnssec-sign \- sign tinydns source as an offline DNSSEC snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dnssec-sign
.RI [ data
.RI [ data.signed ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads one policy line per authoritative zone from
.I dnssec
in the working directory and atomically writes signed tinydns text. It adds
DNSKEY, NSEC, and RRSIG records and rejects unmaterialized ANAME, conditional
records, expiring records, pre-existing DNSSEC data, and policy/zone mismatch.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, 100 for usage errors, and 111 for operational failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnssec-data (1),
.BR dnssec-check (1),
.BR aname-materialize (1)
